ports(8)										   ports(8)

NAME
     ports - update/list ports collection

SYNOPSIS
     ports [options] [collection ...]

DESCRIPTION
     ports  connects  to one or more master repositories and updates the local copy of a ports col‐
     lection. If no collections are specified then all collections will be updated.  A	port  is  a
     directory containing all necessary files for building a software package using pkgmk(8).

OPTIONS
     -u, --update
	    Update ports.

     -l, --list
	    List ports.

     -d, --diff
	    List version differences between local ports and installed packages.

     -v, --version
	    Print version and exit.

     -h, --help
	    Print help and exit.

FILES
     /usr/ports/
	    Root of local ports collection.

     /etc/ports/
	    Directory for port collection configuration.

     /etc/ports/drivers/
	    Directory for driver scripts.

SEE ALSO
     pkgadd(8), pkgrm(8), pkginfo(8)

